    'Super+c            Open VS Code (install first)' \
    'Super+v            Open virt-manager (install first)' \
    'Super+Shift+l      Lock the screen' \
    'Super+Shift+b      Toggle the dwm status bar' \
    'Super+Shift+c      Close focused window' \
    'Super+Shift+q      Exit dwm' \
    '' \
    'Super+j / k        Focus next / previous window in stack' \
    'Super+Down / Up    Focus next / previous window' \
    'Super+Shift+j / k  Move focused window in stack' \
    'Super+Left / Right Move to previous / next tag' \
    'Super+Shift+Left / Right  Move window to previous / next tag' \
    'Super+h / l        Shrink / grow master area' \
    'Super+i / d        Add / remove master window' \
    'Super+Shift+Return Make focused window master' \
    'Super+Tab          View previous tag set' \
    'Super+t / f / m    Tile / floating / monocle layouts' \
    'Super+Space        Cycle layouts' \
    'Super+Shift+Space  Toggle floating for focused window' \
    'Super+0            Show all tags' \
    'Super+1…9          Switch desktop tags' \
    'Super+Shift+1…9    Move window to a tag' \
    'Super+comma / dot  Focus previous / next monitor' \
    'Super+Shift+comma / dot  Move window to previous / next monitor' \
    'Super+Alt+0        Toggle gaps; Super+Alt+Shift+0 resets gaps' \
    'Super+Alt+= / -    Increase / decrease gaps' \
    '' \
    'Super = Windows / Command key. Left Alt remains Alt by default.' \
    'Super+Escape → Settings → Display for monitors, refresh rate, OLED blanking.' \
